  "description": "CR 616.1b three seats: carol is asked WHICH Gather Specimens takes her creature (control)",
  "note": "Three seats, where CR 616.1b's \"one of them must be chosen\" has something to choose between: alice and bob each resolve a Gather Specimens in carol's upkeep, and carol casts Narcomoeba. It would enter under carol's control, an opponent of both, so both rows apply in the same iteration of CR 616.1f. They are equal in effect and differ only in the controller each baked, so CR 616.1 owes the question to the affected object's controller, carol. Her answer inverts the board: the row she names applies, then CR 616.1f re-collects, where the other row sees an opponent's creature again and the named one is spent (CR 614.5), so the creature settles with the player she did NOT name. The control leg: she names bob's row and alice keeps it, so the two runs disagree.",
